  "Question": "What is the maximum value of \\(y=2\\sin x\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "2",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(A=2>0\\), so the maximum value is the amplitude, \\(2\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Bound the sine and attain the bound\n\nThe sine function never exceeds \\(1\\), so \\(2\\sin x\\le2\\) for every real \\(x\\). At \\(x=\\pi/2\\), \\(\\sin x=1\\), so this bound is attained. Therefore the maximum value is \\(2\\).",
